  "body": "cf. https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1236979 and https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1236930. \n\nA popular mapping library, Leaflet.js, when it tests for transitionEnd event prefixes prefers  `webkitTransitionEnd` because some Android browsers had unprefixed CSS `transition` but not an unprefixed `transitionEnd` event. :sob: \n\nIt seems in order to be compatible with this content&mdash;for UAs that do alias `-webkit-transition`&mdash; they need to also send `webkitTransitionEnd` events. Boo.\n\nSee https://github.com/Leaflet/Leaflet/issues/1182 and associated commit.\n",
